# Negating a string and `not` of a number.
mode: check
schema: 'orders.csv'(orderId: string, customerId: string, amount: real, qty: long, small: int, timestamp: datetime, wait: timespan, shipped: bool)
---- query
from 'orders.csv' | where -orderId > 0;
from 'orders.csv' | where not qty
---- expected
error[DS2003]: cannot negate `string`
  --> query:1:28
  |
1 | from 'orders.csv' | where -orderId > 0;
  |                            ^^^^^^^ this is `string` (column `orderId` was read from orders.csv)
  |
  = help: if `orderId` holds numbers, convert it first: `-toreal(orderId)`

error[DS2003]: `not` needs a `bool`, found `long`
  --> query:2:31
  |
2 | from 'orders.csv' | where not qty
  |                               ^^^ this is `long` (column `qty` was read from orders.csv)
